ed12e7c5 MSL: workgroup memory zero-initialization strides by the declared workgroup size, without declaring gl_WorkGroupSize. Declaring it (the previous fix) turned a LocalSizeId workgroup size into a WorkgroupSize constant composite, which MoltenVK read as specialization constants and a threadgroup of 1 thread: DXVK compute shaders with groupshared memory ran one thread per group
42a7589f MSL: zero-initialized workgroup memory declares gl_WorkGroupSize. emit_workgroup_initialization() strides by gl_WorkGroupSize, but the builtin was only added for emulated subgroups, so a compute shader with zero-initialized groupshared memory and no use of WorkgroupSize of its own failed to compile (Sons of the Forest: 13 compute shaders on DXVK 3.1, which zero-initializes D3D11 groupshared memory)
ab0cb152 MSL: a function parameter standing for a global descriptor array takes the global's size. A runtime array is sized per resource binding, which only the global's ID has, so a function taking an argument buffer's sized sampler array declared it as an undeclared spvDescriptorArray<sampler>: DXVK 3.1's present shader (composite_image and sc_rgb_to_output take its global s_samplers heap) failed to compile and nothing was ever presented
a23a9fa8 MSL: a vertex function's SubgroupLocalInvocationId is the thread's place in the active-lane mask (its lane among simd_prefix_exclusive_sum's active lanes, matching simd_ballot's bits), since vertex functions have no [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]; their subgroup operations already work, and the builtin threw, so Dragon's Dogma 2's depth-only vertex shaders (ballot and broadcast-first wave compaction) failed to convert and the game exited with E_OUTOFMEMORY
0bdbd680 MSL: a function taking a buffer array that aliases another binding takes it as spvDescriptorAliasArray, the type the entry point declares; tessellation control shaders (patch_main) failed to compile (RDR2)
cfc29eec MSL: a mesh pipeline's wrappers pass buffers aliasing one binding as their single shared void* argument, and the aliases are declared once; they passed each alias's local name, which the wrapper doesn't have, and every gathering of the wrapper's arguments declared the aliases again (Ghostrunner's geometry pipelines failed to compile and the game exited out of memory)
d221bf08 MSL: a runtime array of buffers aliasing another binding indexes the base array and casts each loaded pointer (spvDescriptorAliasArray); casting the descriptor array pointer crashed Apple's shader compiler while setting up a mesh stage's inputs (Elden Ring's point-list geometry pipelines)
f030e0e5 MSL: the object stage of a mesh pipeline fetches packed 10:10:10:2 and BGRA vertex attributes, per instance for instance-rate bindings, converts integer storage to the shader's float inputs, names 8-bit elements uchar/char, and passes only the builtins its vertex function takes
d52da0ae MSL: a geometry shader in a mesh pipeline (for_mesh_pipeline) gets its implicit position too
116dfa38 MSL: CullDistance outputs write their local, not a stage-out array Metal doesn't have; ray tracing entry points wrap runtime descriptor arrays in spvDescriptorArray; a geometry shader run as a mesh shader always gets a position, also when it only streams out (Elden Ring's and The Witcher 3's pipelines didn't compile)
b75cf231 MSL: OpArrayLength on a runtime array of buffers without rich descriptors reads the buffer size constants, as robust access does: it threw (VKD3D-Proton's compute pipelines in Red Dead Redemption 2 didn't build)
30794b1d MSL: depth bounds emulation makes a declared but unused gl_FragCoord an entry point input: the test reads it, and it was undeclared (Red Dead Redemption 2's pipelines didn't compile)
13441b9f MSL: option frag_output_base_types, 4 bits per color location giving the attachment's SPIRType::BaseType: a fragment output of another kind of number (float, signed, unsigned) is converted to it, since Metal refuses a pipeline whose output type doesn't match its attachment (D3D12 typeless render targets; Vulkan leaves the values undefined)
7c703fc0 MSL: an output the entry point declares itself (a flattened array copied to the captured output at the end) is not remapped to device storage: its component writes were cast to device pointers from thread memory, which doesn't compile (tessellation vertex shaders)
d0df22eb MSL: tessellation variables with a Component decoration are interface members of their own, and a previous stage's output at a component of a location read only in part is padded for, so a control shader's outputs and the evaluation shader's inputs keep one layout (they threw: God of War Ragnarok's tessellated pipelines)
231a98e2 MSL: only resource variables take their array size from resource bindings, so an open-ended binding at set 0, binding 0 doesn't make stage input arrays unsized
96894c68 MSL: option to call the default transcendentals in NaN-preserving shaders, with a NaN select for sin and cos
15cd513f MSL: inline the NoContraction fadd/fsub/fmul helpers instead of [[clang::optnone]]
3b2ca4c7 MSL: cull distances as clip distances
c58749c6 MSL: layered multiview for tessellation, geometry and mesh shaders
6f548633 MSL: 64-bit atomics on threadgroup memory; emulated 64-bit atomics invalidate forwarded loads
5954761a MSL: transform feedback from geometry shaders run as mesh stages
967d7fb6 MSL: geometry shaders through object/mesh stages: every input topology, output topology, builtins
37b90a31 MSL: transform feedback capture kernels keep their stage outputs in the thread
cf5bfcaf MSL: transform feedback capture for MoltenVK's compute capture stage
dd63f4e0 MSL: sparse residency codes of any integer type
4d7f7032 MSL: emulated depth bounds test against a depth snapshot
af9637c8 MSL: conservative rasterization tier 3: degenerate primitives, FullyCoveredEXT from screen-space barycentrics
ecc3387a MSL: 64-bit image atomics (lock table, device-coherent textures), R64i images as ulong, 64-bit subgroup ops
e4453a5b MSL: conservative-rasterization mesh stage for vertex shaders; mesh wrappers pass argument buffers, base vertex/instance and dynamic strides
984dcd6a MSL: compute-shader derivatives (linear quads via quad_shuffle) and lock-table 64-bit buffer atomics
af803734 MSL: Drop a debug print of the MSL version
4fd3de5b Merge minamorl/SPIRV-Cross 3c567d2b (SPIRV-Cross PR #2654): MSL geometry shaders as mesh stages and transform feedback
02351021 MSL: Emulate min/max sampler reduction
4b0922ca MSL: Support sparse residency feedback
